From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:56:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/27] tides: index the template clusters and prepare
 snapshots once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The detector rehashed every snapshot on every call and compared every
pair of gateways: O(gateways² × snapshots), 233 s per stats build at
240 gateways (SOV-003). Snapshots are now prepared once when recorded
(txids fingerprinted, merkle branches cached), the pool's snapshots are
indexed once per pass, and clusters come from one (parent, branches)
index. The pairwise code stays as entropy::reference, and property
tests hold the new code to it on random worlds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
